ype":"element","tagName":"td","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"65"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"td","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"strong","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"0"}]}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"td","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"91"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"td","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"13"}]},{"type":"element","tagName":"td","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"98"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"¹ Timeout/ExitCode/Setup/Reward/Verifier/NetworkConnectionError — the only category Harbor's own exit-code-based detection actually catches.\n² llama.cpp's PEG parser crash ("},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Failed to parse input at pos N"}]},{"type":"text","value":"), trial ended fatally right there. Zero on vLLM.\n³ OpenHands' "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"AgentStuckInLoopError"}]},{"type":"text","value":" killed the attempt.\n⁴ Other unrelated fatal errors (mostly the "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"chardet"}]},{"type":"text","value":"/action-execution-server bug on vLLM).\n⁵ Attempts that neither resolved, hit a Harbor exception, nor showed any of the fatal patterns checked — genuinely completed but produced a wrong patch, or a crash pattern not yet characterized."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"problem-2-harbor-error-handling","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#problem-2-harbor-error-handling","ariaLabel":"problem 2 harbor error handling permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Problem 2: Harbor error handling"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second problem is that Harbor does not detect the error.  And it seems that\nthis is because openhands returns exit code 0."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a mess!"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h1","properties":{"id":"concluding-thoughts","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#concluding-thoughts","ariaLabel":"concluding thoughts permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Concluding Thoughts"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"We can't detect the redundant "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"<thinking>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" tag problem in vllm, but it could\nstill be happening.  vllm has a different tool parsing mechanism than llama.cpp;\nit might be more forgiving.  For whatever reason, vllm-thinking is still\nunderperforming vllm-nonthinking."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"h2","properties":{"id":"next-steps","style":"position:relative;"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"a","properties":{"href":"#next-steps","ariaLabel":"next steps permalink","className":["anchor","before"]},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"svg","properties":{"ariaHidden":"true","focusable":"false","height":"16","version":"1.1","viewBox":"0 0 16 16","width":"16"},"children":[{"type":"element","tagName":"path","properties":{"fillRule":"evenodd","d":"M4 9h1v1H4c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5S2.55 3 4 3h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-.91 2.72-2 3.25V8.59c.58-.45 1-1.27 1-2.09C10 5.22 8.98 4 8 4H4c-.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5S3 9 4 9zm9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5S13.98 12 13 12H9c-.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-.83.42-1.64 1-2.09V6.25c-1.09.53-2 1.84-2 3.25C6 11.31 7.55 13 9 13h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5S14.5 6 13 6z"},"children":[]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I am going to try to confirm whether the redundant "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"<thinking>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" tag is generated\nby vllm-thinking.  If it is, then it suggests that the model is buggy.  Which\nwould be weird --- the model defaults to thinking.  (Update: I confirmed that\nvllm-thinking "},{"type":"element","tagName":"em","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"does"}]},{"type":"text","value":" generate the redundant "},{"type":"element","tagName":"code","properties":{"className":["language-text"]},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"<thinking>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" tag, but its parser\nmust be more forgiving than llama.cpp's parser.)"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"I am also going to investigate agents other than openhands.  I originally\nselected openhands because it is the first agent I was able to get to work with\nHarbor.  But at the time, Harbor was only compatible with an older branch of\nopenhands.  Hopefully this has changed, or a more reasonable harness like\nopencode will work now."}]},{"type":"text","value":"\n"},{"type":"element","tagName":"p","properties":{},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"At this point, I'm getting pretty tired of debugging this model.  I think the\nnext step is to try a different model; I am thinking about trying gemma4 next."}]}],"data":{"quirksMode":false}},"excerpt":"In Part\n1\nand Part\n2,\nI reported some peculiar behavior for quantized Qwen3.5-2B models.  In Part 3,\nI reported results for a larger variant…","timeToRead":4,"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2026-07-22--benchmarking-quantized-ll-ms-for-local-coding-agents-part-4-investigating-the-impact-of-thinking-on-qwen3-5-35-b-a3-b/"},"frontmatter":{"tags":["llm","ai","autobench"],"author":{"jsonId":"Edward J. Schwartz","bio":"Computer Security Researcher","twitter":"@edmcman","avatar":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"fixed","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png","srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/4ed6d/ed.png 80w","sizes":"80px"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/b0e73023d6a6055546d8e671edd67950/1deab/ed.webp 80w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"80px"}]},"widt